    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0695" n="593" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins Notes</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d377-f1"
                    /></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-chapter-heading" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1943-12-01T13:00:00+03:25">December 1, 1943, 1 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>1. Turkey should be asked to come into the war &amp; invite President of Turkey
                    to come to Cairo to meet the President of U. S. A. &amp; Prime Minister.</p>
                <p>Mr. Eden asked Marshall [<hi rendition="#italic">Marshal</hi>] Stalin whether the
                    Soviet Government wished to send a representative—if so he would of course be
                    welcomed.</p>
                <p>M. Stalin answered that he would send such a representative.</p>
                <p>Proposed telegram to Pres. Inonu was presented and discussed.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d377-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d377-f1-content">
                <p>These notes, in Hopkins’ handwriting, are headed “Mr. Eden[’s] report of Foreign
                    Minister Committee”. The material reproduced here ends at the middle of a page
                    and appears to be incomplete. No other Hopkins notes of this meeting have been
                    found.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
